==English==

===Etymology===
From {{af|en|octo-|-phobia}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-}}

# The [[irrational]] [[fear]] of the number [[eight]].
#* {{quote-web|en|author=Rajendra Kunwar|title=MATHEMATICS PHOBIA: CAUSES, SYMPTOMS AND WAYS TO OVERCOME|url=https://www.ijcrt.org/papers/IJCRT2008103.pdf|date=2020-08|volume=8|issue=8|issn=2320-2882|page=820|work=International Journal of Creative Research Thoughts|passage=Country like Nepal, India, Bhutan and Myanmar, people who follows Hindu religion, they consider the numbers 0, 1, 8, 10, 12, 19 and 28 as unlucky numbers, bad luck or evil spirits etc. These numbers are called oudenophobia, henophobia, '''octophobia''', decaphobia, dodecaphobia, enneadecaphobia and eikosioctophobia respectively.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|title=Octophobia (Fear of the Number 8)|magazine=Cleaveland Clinic|url=https://my.clevelandclinic.org/health/diseases/22539-octophobia-fear-of-the-number-8|date=2022-03-22|passage=People with '''octophobia''' experience anxiety when they think about or see the number 8.}}

